values ('f9a0b1c2-3d4e-4a39-8b89-0c1d2e3f4a99', 'introduction-to-criminal-justice', 'Introduction to Criminal Justice', 'Introduction to Criminal Justice treats the field as linked institutions, decisions, values, and consequences. Students trace U.S. history, constitutional foundations, crime measurement, and criminological theory, then study policing, courts, corrections, victims, youth development, inequality, policy, ethics, evidence, technology, comparative and public health approaches, careers, and evidence-based reform.');

